@startuml ClassModel
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Class Model — produced by the Developer at M3.
'
' This is the DETAILED static model. Distinct from `domain-model.puml`:
'   - Domain model = real-world entities, attributes only, project glossary.
'     Owned: PO at M1 (initial), Analyst at M2 (refinement).
'   - Class model = implementation classes with attributes + OPERATIONS,
'     including framework / DI / repository / orchestrator classes that
'     don't appear on the domain model. Owned: Developer at M3.
'
' Save as `class-model/class-model.puml` at the project root.
'
' Rules:
'   1. Every class referenced on a sequence diagram (SD-XXX) must
'      appear here. The CDR readiness check enforces this.
'   2. Every operation on a class must be allocated to it via an SD
'      message arrow (one method per arrow per Developer rule 5).
'   3. Attributes MUST be typed. Untyped attributes (`+ name` with no
'      `: type`) are M3 blockers (Reviewer check #2 — "attribute untyped").
'   4. Entity classes (the ones that came from the domain model) need
'      ≥1 attribute even if the framework typically generates them via
'      ORM. Attribute-sparse entities (≥2 operations and 0 attributes)
'      are flagged by the Reviewer.
'   5. Use stereotypes to make architectural roles visible:
'        <<entity>>      — domain entity
'        <<controller>>  — orchestrator (MVC controller, application service)
'        <<repository>>  — persistence-adapter interface or impl
'        <<service>>     — Application-layer interface (DI)
'        <<value>>       — value object (no identity)
'        <<external>>    — third-party library / framework type used as a lifeline
'   6. Show interface ↔ implementation pairs for DI-introduced types
'      (e.g., ICurrentUserService → CookieCurrentUserService). Reviewer
'      check #6 looks for framework concerns mixed into business logic;
'      visible interface boundaries help.
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' >>> REPLACE THE EXAMPLE BELOW WITH YOUR PROJECT'S CLASSES. <<<
' >>> The example shows the Internet Bookstore stack (.NET).         <<<
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

' ── Boundary / orchestrator (Web layer) ───────────────────────────
class WriteCustomerReviewController <<controller>> {
  + WriteAsync(bookId : int) : ActionResult
  + SubmitAsync(review : CustomerReview) : ActionResult
}

' ── Domain entities (came from domain model; attributes typed) ────
class CustomerReview <<entity>> {
  + id : int
  + bookId : int
  + customerId : int
  + reviewText : string
  + rating : int
  + status : ReviewStatus
  + Validate(context : ValidationContext) : IEnumerable<ValidationResult>
}

class Book <<entity>> {
  + id : int
  + title : string
}

class CustomerSession <<entity>> {
  + customerId : int
  + isLoggedIn : bool
}

' ── Application-layer interfaces (DI; introduced per Developer rule 4) ─
interface ICurrentUserService <<service>> {
  + GetSession(httpContext : HttpContext) : CustomerSession
}

class CookieCurrentUserService <<service>> {
  ' Implementation; lives in Bookstore.Application.
}

' ── Repository interfaces + implementations ──────────────────────
interface IBookRepository <<repository>> {
  + GetByIdAsync(id : int) : Task<Book>
  + Exists(id : int) : bool
}

class EfBookRepository <<repository>> {
  ' Implementation; lives in Bookstore.Infrastructure.
}

interface ICustomerReviewRepository <<repository>> {
  + AddAsync(review : CustomerReview) : Task<CustomerReview>
}

class EfCustomerReviewRepository <<repository>> {
}

' ── Async-output adapter ──────────────────────────────────────────
interface IPendingReviewsQueue <<repository>> {
  + EnqueueAsync(reviewId : int) : Task
}

class BusPendingReviewsQueue <<repository>> {
}

' ── Relationships ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
WriteCustomerReviewController --> ICurrentUserService : uses
WriteCustomerReviewController --> IBookRepository : uses
WriteCustomerReviewController --> ICustomerReviewRepository : uses
WriteCustomerReviewController --> IPendingReviewsQueue : uses

CookieCurrentUserService ..|> ICurrentUserService
EfBookRepository ..|> IBookRepository
EfCustomerReviewRepository ..|> ICustomerReviewRepository
BusPendingReviewsQueue ..|> IPendingReviewsQueue

CustomerReview "0..*" --> "1" Book : references
CustomerReview "0..*" --> "1" CustomerSession : created by

note bottom
  Traceability:
    UC: PREFIX-UC-XXX
    SDs that reference these classes: PREFIX-SD-XXX
    Domain entities here came from: domain-model/domain-model.puml
    DI interfaces justified in: container-mapping/PREFIX-UC-XXX-containers.md
end note

@enduml
